WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:17.640
 Part of what I was trying to do with that piece was capture that feeling of the way something tastes that you might have grown up eating, it just tastes totally different in a different place.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:32.140
 We were sitting in the living room and, you know, I don't know why there were limes, but I was like, I'm going to cut one and, you know, eat it, and I eat it like some Persians do, like, squeeze the juice into my mouth and then gum it and teethe it and then you turn it inside out and eat the whole pulp.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:48.160
 And I was just there doing that and my uncle was like, are these great, you know, and I said, yeah, you know, this is, and they taste amazing, they've always tasted amazing, but they taste a certain way here, you know, they just have that, it's like, yes, you're never going to taste like this in the States.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.660
 And I was thinking, yeah, that's so funny, we get so proud about food, but at the same time, he was totally right.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:01:04.140
 And, oh, and what I remembered, I remember doing that in that same living room and my aunt, my mom's older sister, talking to me and saying, don't start doing that.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.920
 I did, I've done that all my life and it's just going to ruin your teeth.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.440
 But she's like smiling while she says it, she knows, like, and she just, you're going to want to do it.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:18.340
 So there's, of course, you know, food and family and love, it's all, it's all like packed in there.

